          "snippet": {
            "text": "/-- **Gauss sum of an induced character**: for `f` periodic mod `N`, completely multiplicative,\nand zero off the residues coprime to `N`,\n`Σ_{b < Nr, (b, Nr) = 1} f(b) e(b/Nr) = μ(r) f(r) Σ_{c < N} f(c) e(c/N)`. -/\ntheorem gauss_induced {N r : ℕ} (hN : 1 ≤ N) (hr : 1 ≤ r) (f : ℕ → ℂ)\n    (hper : ∀ b, f (b + N) = f b) (hmul : ∀ a b, f (a * b) = f a * f b)\n    (hzero : ∀ b, ¬ Nat.Coprime b N → f b = 0) :\n    ∑ b ∈ (range (N * r)).filter (fun b => Nat.Coprime b (N * r)), f b * e (b / (N * r)) =\n      μ r * f r * ∑ c ∈ range N, f c * e (c / N) := by",
            "line": 66,
            "truncated": false
          },
          "proof_context": {
            "declaration": "TernaryGoldbach.gauss_induced",
            "lines": [
              66,
              143
            ],
            "conclusion": "Gauss sum of an induced character: $\\sum_{b<Nr,(b,Nr)=1}f(b)e(b/Nr)=\\mu(r)f(r)\\sum_{c<N}f(c)e(c/N)$."
          },
